The film is based on Matthew Quick's 2008 novel The Silver Linings Playbook.

14
01:05:41,538 --> 01:05:47,538
It stars Bradley Cooper and Jennifer Lawrence, with Robert De Niro, Jacki
Weaver, Anupam Kher, and Chris Tucker in supporting roles.

15
01:10:23,076 --> 01:10:29,076
The film is set in Lansdowne, Pennsylvania.

16
01:15:04,615 --> 01:15:10,615
Cooper plays Patrizio "Pat" Solitano Jr., a man with bipolar disorder who is released from
a psychiatric hospital and moves in with his parents (De Niro and Weaver).

17
01:19:46,153 --> 01:19:52,153
Pat is determined to restore the love of his estranged wife.

18
01:24:27,692 --> 01:24:33,692
He meets a young widow, Tiffany Maxwell (Lawrence), who offers to
help him if he enters a dance competition with her.

19
01:29:09,230 --> 01:29:15,230
The two become closer as they train, and Pat, his father, and Tiffany examine their
relationships with each other as they cope with their situations.

20
01:33:50,769 --> 01:33:56,769
Silver Linings Playbook premiered at the 2012 Toronto International Film Festival on September 8, 2012,
and was released in the United States by The Weinstein Company on November 16, 2012.

21
01:38:32,307 --> 01:38:38,307
